      "body": "Allow fixed-window DSpARK KDA verification with 9–16 tokens to use the existing CuTe fused kernel instead of falling back. Existing eligibility checks remain unchanged. Extend the output-normalization test to cover windows 8, 9, 12, and 16.\n\nWith public Kimi-K3 on B300 TP8, a 9-token verify window, 8192 input tokens, 1024 output tokens, and simulated acceptance length 4, three-run median steady decode throughput increased from 234.11 to 243.04 tok/s at batch 1 (+3.81%) and from 924.42 to 976.24 tok/s at batch 8 (+5.61%). These are performance measurements, not accuracy validation, and were collected before the final rebase onto current main.\n\nThe added long-window GPU test cases have not yet been run. Python syntax and diff checks pass.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40840497627](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40840497627)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40840497602](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40840497602)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40840497681](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40840497681)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
